1
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:05,720
Taming The Husband

2
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:08,720
Episode 15

3
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:38,720
How are you going to punish me?

4
00:01:40,880 --> 00:01:41,920
You… you're not drunk?

5
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:30,160
Spare me, Your Majesty!

6
00:02:30,720 --> 00:02:31,720
Not a chance.

7
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:42,680
Lady Jin, the rules say

8
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:45,920
a concubine can't stay
in the principal room overnight.

9
00:02:46,760 --> 00:02:49,280
You must… you must…

10
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:51,160
you must go back to your room.

11
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:54,760
Right! That's what I thought.

12
00:03:09,160 --> 00:03:11,600
But promise me, no more breaking things.

13
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,280
Get out!

14
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:07,520
Mother.

15
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:16,320
Father.

16
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:20,480
Your father and I need to talk,

17
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:23,000
so tonight,
you'll have to make do in the side room.

18
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:25,040
Go wash your face and get some sleep.

19
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:26,240
Stop!

20
00:04:27,040 --> 00:04:28,360
Chanyue, leave us.

21
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:32,480
Didn't you hear me telling you to leave?

22
00:04:34,320 --> 00:04:35,320
Out!

23
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:39,360
Don't worry.

24
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:50,400
Father.

25
00:04:50,640 --> 00:04:51,640
Kneel!

26
00:04:56,680 --> 00:04:57,880
Why are you angry, Father?

27
00:04:58,520 --> 00:04:59,520
Why?

28
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:02,000
You dare ask me that?

29
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:04,840
I gave you life and raised you,

30
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:07,120
saving the best of everything for you,

31
00:05:07,320 --> 00:05:08,480
because I want you to succeed

32
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:10,240
and inherit the business!

33
00:05:11,840 --> 00:05:12,840
And you?

34
00:05:13,080 --> 00:05:15,200
You go drinking with Xie Chengzong's son!

35
00:05:15,400 --> 00:05:17,120
Trying to kill your father?

36
00:05:19,480 --> 00:05:20,680
We're one family,

37
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:22,320
so his success is ours, too.

38
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:27,960
I'll teach you to talk back!

39
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:32,240
Do you understand what's at stake?

40
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:34,040
Despite all our plotting these past days,

41
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:35,720
we still couldn't bring Yan down!

42
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:37,560
He works under me,

43
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:39,360
but now he's sailing tomorrow,

44
00:05:40,040 --> 00:05:41,360
and the money I've worked so hard for

45
00:05:41,440 --> 00:05:42,680
has to be shared with him!

46
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:45,640
How's that any different from robbery?

47
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:47,400
You could open new routes,

48
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:50,320
instead of fighting
Uncle Chengzong tooth and nail.

49
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:54,200
Grandmother would be upset, too.

50
00:05:54,280 --> 00:05:55,680
Think I don't know that?

51
00:05:58,320 --> 00:05:59,600
If it were that easy,

52
00:05:59,960 --> 00:06:01,400
I'd have done it long ago!

53
00:06:01,880 --> 00:06:03,080
But they managed it.

54
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:05,320
You-- Fine!

55
00:06:05,560 --> 00:06:06,800
You'll be the death of me!

56
00:06:06,880 --> 00:06:08,400
Go on, kill your father!

57
00:06:08,480 --> 00:06:09,600
I'll beat you to death!

58
00:06:10,280 --> 00:06:11,320
Beat you to death! I…

59
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:26,400
Do something for me.

60
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:28,240
When Xie Yan sails,

61
00:06:29,160 --> 00:06:30,600
help me keep him away.

62
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:34,920
I won't.

63
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:37,920
-I'll kill you!
-Xie Rongchang!

64
00:06:42,520 --> 00:06:43,520
Get up.

65
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:45,520
-My lord.
-Careful.

66
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:49,760
Why didn't you dodge?

67
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:54,320
He's my father.

68
00:06:56,400 --> 00:06:57,520
Foolish child.

69
00:06:58,400 --> 00:06:59,520
Help him down.

70
00:06:59,600 --> 00:07:00,600
Yes.

71
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:02,480
Careful.

72
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:12,320
Take your anger out on me!

73
00:07:12,920 --> 00:07:14,560
Beat me to death if you dare!

74
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:17,880
This is my child,

75
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:20,240
and I want my child to live with dignity.

76
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:22,560
If you want dirty tricks,

77
00:07:22,640 --> 00:07:23,720
fine! I'll do them!

78
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:24,800
You--

79
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:31,320
A doting mother ruins her child!

80
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:54,840
What are you doing?

81
00:07:55,880 --> 00:07:57,120
With the river so rough,

82
00:07:57,680 --> 00:08:00,120
I'm making pills for nausea and dizziness.

83
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:04,920
I've been away so many times,

84
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:07,000
and you still worry.

85
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:10,360
Silly woman.

86
00:08:14,880 --> 00:08:16,840
I'll be away for a long time on this trip.

87
00:08:17,720 --> 00:08:20,280
Anything you'd like me to bring back?

88
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:28,920
These are for Yan.

89
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:31,080
Who's silly now?

90
00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:35,800
Take it.

91
00:08:42,760 --> 00:08:43,920
If you don't understand something,

92
00:08:44,160 --> 00:08:46,360
ask people and learn from them,

93
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:47,800
or just write to me.

94
00:08:47,920 --> 00:08:48,920
Send your letters to the docks,

95
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:50,640
and someone will bring them to me.

96
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:52,800
Writing's such a bother!

97
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:54,280
You're on a short route,

98
00:08:54,360 --> 00:08:55,680
so you'll be back in five or six days!

99
00:08:55,960 --> 00:08:57,600
That's 15 or 16 autumns!

100
00:08:57,680 --> 00:08:58,680
Why?

101
00:09:00,160 --> 00:09:02,680
"A day apart is like three autumns."

102
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:04,440
Stop it.

103
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:06,040
I'm warning you,

104
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:07,680
if you dare

105
00:09:07,760 --> 00:09:09,840
hire singing girls on that boat,
I'll sink it!

106
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:12,200
Not my legs this time?

107
00:09:13,520 --> 00:09:16,080
I… I was drunk yesterday.

108
00:09:17,160 --> 00:09:19,720
Unfortunately, I wasn't.

109
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:29,480
No goodbye?

110
00:09:45,640 --> 00:09:46,760
My lord, we'll be late!

111
00:09:46,840 --> 00:09:48,160
We… we have to--

112
00:09:54,080 --> 00:09:56,160
Right! Hurry, or you'll be late!

113
00:10:00,280 --> 00:10:01,280
I'll go, then.

114
00:10:17,040 --> 00:10:19,200
Remember, write to me.

115
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:32,360
THE VAST SEA

116
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:33,480
Take care of yourself.

117
00:10:40,600 --> 00:10:42,560
-Six of characters.
-Mahjong!

118
00:10:42,800 --> 00:10:44,760
Why'd you play that?
He keeps winning!

119
00:10:46,120 --> 00:10:47,240
Such good luck!

120
00:10:47,320 --> 00:10:49,080
The authorities are cracking down,

121
00:10:49,480 --> 00:10:51,040
holding up shipments,

122
00:10:51,120 --> 00:10:52,880
so of course salt prices are rising!

123
00:10:53,480 --> 00:10:54,760
Put the price too high,

124
00:10:54,840 --> 00:10:55,880
and who'll buy stock?

125
00:10:55,960 --> 00:10:58,600
Carriers like us
will be the first to starve.

126
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:02,000
-Forget it!
-I heard a new route's opened,

127
00:11:02,160 --> 00:11:04,680
so we'll have plenty of work,
even more than before!

128
00:11:04,760 --> 00:11:05,880
Have they really opened a new route?

129
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:07,400
-Is it true?
-Assemble!

130
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:08,920
My boss is calling, so you keep playing!

131
00:11:09,320 --> 00:11:11,840
Come on, assemble! Quick! Quick! Quick!

132
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:14,720
What's wrong?
Gone weak at the knees on dry land?

133
00:11:16,080 --> 00:11:17,080
Hurry!

134
00:11:21,400 --> 00:11:23,560
Your orders, my lord?

135
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:29,120
This time,

136
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:31,280
we leave Lianhua Station in Yangzhou

137
00:11:31,360 --> 00:11:32,560
on a short-haul grain run,

138
00:11:32,640 --> 00:11:34,280
to Changying Granary in Huaizhou.

139
00:11:34,760 --> 00:11:36,760
Once you've safely delivered the grain

140
00:11:36,920 --> 00:11:38,120
and it's been inspected and received,

141
00:11:38,840 --> 00:11:40,240
your job is done.

142
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:43,480
I won't say any more,

143
00:11:43,920 --> 00:11:45,360
but I'm counting on you all.

144
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:49,040
Do well, and there's a reward
when we get back.

145
00:11:49,680 --> 00:11:53,360
-A reward!
-A reward? Really?

146
00:11:55,400 --> 00:11:56,400
Dismissed.

147
00:11:56,920 --> 00:11:59,320
We sail in exactly fifteen minutes!

148
00:12:22,920 --> 00:12:24,240
In fifteen minutes,

149
00:12:25,120 --> 00:12:26,760
we set sail, on the dot!

150
00:12:29,640 --> 00:12:30,640
Yes!

151
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:35,160
Let's work hard, then.

152
00:12:35,240 --> 00:12:36,240
First Master Xie didn't want us,

153
00:12:36,680 --> 00:12:37,840
but we can find work elsewhere.

154
00:12:38,080 --> 00:12:40,120
But since we used to
work under First Master Xie,

155
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:41,320
will he really trust us?

156
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:45,280
Perhaps he's looking for an excuse
to throw us out.

157
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:47,000
Enough.

158
00:12:48,120 --> 00:12:49,720
Just do your job properly.

159
00:12:50,320 --> 00:12:51,320
Aboard!

160
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:55,080
My lord.

161
00:12:57,880 --> 00:12:58,880
Let's go.

162
00:13:07,280 --> 00:13:08,280
YAN

163
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:11,000
XIE

164
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:44,400
XIE

165
00:13:49,720 --> 00:13:52,240
XIE

166
00:13:59,320 --> 00:14:00,480
I'm bored.

167
00:14:02,280 --> 00:14:03,880
Making money, and you're bored?

168
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:07,200
Are you ill?

169
00:14:07,440 --> 00:14:10,280
Stop it!
Think all I care about is money?

170
00:14:11,960 --> 00:14:13,080
Can I ask you something?

171
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:17,440
Never mind. It's personal.

172
00:14:17,520 --> 00:14:18,600
Go on.

173
00:14:21,040 --> 00:14:24,560
I have a friend, and lately,

174
00:14:24,880 --> 00:14:27,160
she can't stop thinking about someone.

175
00:14:28,760 --> 00:14:30,400
<i>He's rather good-looking,</i>

176
00:14:30,760 --> 00:14:31,960
My lord, the seasickness pills.

177
00:14:35,640 --> 00:14:36,640
Water.

178
00:14:40,960 --> 00:14:42,480
<i>but has a bit of a temper.</i>

179
00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:46,160
Not linen,

180
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:47,400
it's too rough on my mouth!

181
00:14:47,640 --> 00:14:48,840
I want Shu brocade.

182
00:14:49,120 --> 00:14:51,440
My lord, we're miles from anywhere,

183
00:14:51,640 --> 00:14:52,640
and this is all we've got,

184
00:14:52,720 --> 00:14:53,840
so please make do.

185
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:55,240
No! I won't use it!

186
00:14:56,720 --> 00:14:57,720
Young Master Xie,

187
00:14:58,000 --> 00:14:59,040
if Lady Jin knew

188
00:14:59,120 --> 00:15:00,640
how picky you're being,

189
00:15:00,840 --> 00:15:02,400
what would she say?

190
00:15:02,480 --> 00:15:03,600
Using her against me?

191
00:15:05,360 --> 00:15:06,440
Think I'm afraid of her?

192
00:15:11,280 --> 00:15:12,840
<i>Still so proud!</i>

193
00:15:16,640 --> 00:15:17,640
Wait.

194
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:18,960
Come back.

195
00:15:20,960 --> 00:15:22,160
My lord, that's had vomit on it!

196
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:23,240
You wouldn't normally use it.

197
00:15:23,320 --> 00:15:24,800
We brought plenty, so it's all right.

198
00:15:25,280 --> 00:15:26,600
Have this washed and use it again.

199
00:15:26,880 --> 00:15:27,880
The rest…

200
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:29,720
the rest of the linen,

201
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:30,840
share it among the men.

202
00:15:31,560 --> 00:15:34,320
My lord, it's hard to come by!
They're only a bunch of--

203
00:15:34,400 --> 00:15:36,160
Uncle Rongchang
may have cast them off,

204
00:15:36,400 --> 00:15:37,400
but they know their work.

205
00:15:37,560 --> 00:15:38,760
Help them a little,

206
00:15:39,680 --> 00:15:40,760
and we may win them over.

207
00:15:41,800 --> 00:15:44,920
<i>But, he's slowly learning</i>

208
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:46,800
to admit his mistakes
and make up for them.

209
00:15:46,920 --> 00:15:47,960
-So--
-I see.

210
00:15:48,160 --> 00:15:51,760
This friend of yours is beyond saving.

211
00:15:51,920 --> 00:15:53,040
Why?

212
00:15:53,840 --> 00:15:57,680
Because she's fallen in love.

213
00:15:59,280 --> 00:16:01,720
She… she can swim!

214
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:03,360
Swimming won't help!

215
00:16:03,480 --> 00:16:05,000
Wait till the flood comes!

216
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:09,440
This is getting sickeningly sweet.

217
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:15,400
I… I was on my way,

218
00:16:15,480 --> 00:16:16,640
and they… they wanted to see you.

219
00:16:16,720 --> 00:16:18,480
Manager Jin, it's been a while.

220
00:16:18,560 --> 00:16:19,840
Remember us?

221
00:16:21,320 --> 00:16:22,560
Of course,

222
00:16:22,680 --> 00:16:25,200
you're some of our biggest customers.

223
00:16:25,320 --> 00:16:26,320
At this late hour,

224
00:16:26,680 --> 00:16:27,960
what brings you here?

225
00:16:28,040 --> 00:16:29,280
Why don't we sit and talk?

226
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:35,840
Fine.
We'll let her go if you'll serve us tea.

227
00:16:37,720 --> 00:16:38,880
Some of the Bai family

228
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:41,000
are in the salt trade.

229
00:16:41,120 --> 00:16:43,720
They used to buy from you.

230
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:44,800
Now there's trouble,

231
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:47,840
and as their elder brother,
I have to get justice for them.

232
00:16:47,920 --> 00:16:50,680
I happened to run into these gentlemen,

233
00:16:51,040 --> 00:16:52,920
and they chose me to lead them

234
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:54,960
in a little talk with you.

235
00:16:57,040 --> 00:16:59,880
You are in trouble.

236
00:17:00,840 --> 00:17:01,840
Bring it up!

237
00:17:06,560 --> 00:17:08,040
The government allocates

238
00:17:08,120 --> 00:17:09,880
a fixed number of salt permits.

239
00:17:10,640 --> 00:17:12,000
A shop this size

240
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:15,400
should have 3,000.

241
00:17:15,640 --> 00:17:17,320
Yes. So?

242
00:17:18,200 --> 00:17:19,200
But we've bought

243
00:17:19,280 --> 00:17:21,400
salt permits from you
to the tune of 2,000!

244
00:17:21,480 --> 00:17:22,920
Not counting those held by small buyers,

245
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:24,160
or sold at other times!

246
00:17:24,240 --> 00:17:26,960
Haven't you oversold your permits?

247
00:17:34,040 --> 00:17:36,000
Overselling salt permits
is a serious crime,

248
00:17:36,080 --> 00:17:37,360
-isn't it?
-Yes!

249
00:17:37,440 --> 00:17:39,800
But we're kind men,

250
00:17:40,360 --> 00:17:41,520
so we could let you off,

251
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:42,840
as long as you

252
00:17:42,920 --> 00:17:44,320
buy them back at the original price.

253
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:46,040
Otherwise, we go to court!

254
00:17:46,520 --> 00:17:48,240
You'll go to prison,

255
00:17:48,320 --> 00:17:49,680
and the Xies will suffer, too!

256
00:17:49,760 --> 00:17:50,920
None of you will get away with it!

257
00:17:53,320 --> 00:17:54,320
Well?

258
00:17:54,720 --> 00:17:57,320
If you can't find that much money at once,

259
00:17:57,400 --> 00:18:00,160
why not bow and admit your fault?

260
00:18:00,440 --> 00:18:02,160
We might give you another

261
00:18:02,240 --> 00:18:03,480
10 days or two weeks.

262
00:18:03,720 --> 00:18:05,360
Want to go to prison?

263
00:18:05,840 --> 00:18:07,360
I'll go beat the petition drum!

264
00:18:07,800 --> 00:18:09,000
Too proud to bow?

265
00:18:09,240 --> 00:18:10,360
-Then off to prison with you!
-You are in trouble.

266
00:18:10,600 --> 00:18:11,760
Calm down, gentlemen.

267
00:18:11,880 --> 00:18:12,920
I'll bow to you.

268
00:18:18,120 --> 00:18:19,120
Good.

269
00:18:20,040 --> 00:18:21,040
Go and report me,

270
00:18:21,640 --> 00:18:23,640
have me arrested, even beheaded!

271
00:18:24,160 --> 00:18:25,160
Go on!

272
00:18:25,560 --> 00:18:27,640
What… what are you doing?

273
00:18:27,720 --> 00:18:29,640
If you've given up, no one's stopping you.

274
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:32,600
But think of the shop assistants!

275
00:18:33,640 --> 00:18:34,760
If you're not stopping me,

276
00:18:34,840 --> 00:18:36,400
why try to talk me out of it?

277
00:18:36,640 --> 00:18:39,560
I… I have a conscience!

278
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:41,680
You have a conscience?

279
00:18:41,760 --> 00:18:42,880
You… you…

280
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,800
Bai Junmei, you have no conscience!

281
00:18:49,200 --> 00:18:51,120
If the Bais aren't friends of the Xies,

282
00:18:51,280 --> 00:18:52,680
why go so easy on me,

283
00:18:52,760 --> 00:18:54,320
even giving me a chance

284
00:18:54,480 --> 00:18:55,920
to buy back these permits?

285
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:59,160
Did your own gamble go wrong?

286
00:18:59,960 --> 00:19:01,240
What… what are you saying?

287
00:19:01,560 --> 00:19:02,840
Word was going around

288
00:19:02,920 --> 00:19:03,960
that salt prices would rise,

289
00:19:04,520 --> 00:19:05,640
bringing salt merchants

290
00:19:05,720 --> 00:19:07,640
here to snap up permits,

291
00:19:07,800 --> 00:19:08,880
so you raised prices

292
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:10,200
and made a fortune.

293
00:19:10,280 --> 00:19:12,240
But yesterday, the news changed,

294
00:19:12,360 --> 00:19:14,280
and our permits became worthless paper!

295
00:19:14,360 --> 00:19:16,080
-That's right!
-Worthless!

296
00:19:16,240 --> 00:19:18,360
You've pocketed our silver!

297
00:19:18,440 --> 00:19:19,440
Of course we want it back!

298
00:19:19,520 --> 00:19:20,720
-Exactly!
-That's right!

299
00:19:20,800 --> 00:19:22,640
-How could we--
-First, scarcity drives up prices,

300
00:19:22,840 --> 00:19:24,640
and the rise in salt prices
has nothing to do with me.

301
00:19:24,720 --> 00:19:26,960
Second, you chose to hoard salt permits,

302
00:19:27,040 --> 00:19:28,120
so accept the loss

303
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:29,520
instead of coming to me for money!

304
00:19:29,680 --> 00:19:32,160
You're using those oversold permits

305
00:19:32,280 --> 00:19:33,840
to make me clean up your mess!

306
00:19:34,680 --> 00:19:35,680
No!

307
00:19:35,960 --> 00:19:38,680
You should be serving me tea!

308
00:19:38,760 --> 00:19:39,760
What?

309
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:42,200
Scared out of your mind?

310
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:46,600
A permit used to cost four taels,

311
00:19:47,400 --> 00:19:49,920
so 100 permits,
stacked four fingers thick,

312
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:51,320
came to 400 taels.

313
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:52,960
With four stacks per layer in your chest

314
00:19:53,040 --> 00:19:54,360
and a height of 21 fingers,

315
00:19:54,760 --> 00:19:56,240
that's 2,100 permits,

316
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:57,520
or 8,400 taels.

317
00:19:58,200 --> 00:20:00,240
If I owe you 70 or 80 taels,
you own me,

318
00:20:00,320 --> 00:20:01,440
but if it's seven or eight thousand,

319
00:20:01,520 --> 00:20:02,960
I own you!

320
00:20:03,840 --> 00:20:04,840
My life's worth nothing,

321
00:20:05,120 --> 00:20:06,280
so I can just jump in the river

322
00:20:06,960 --> 00:20:07,960
and my debts will die with me.

323
00:20:08,240 --> 00:20:11,200
But you?
You'll still be holding the permits!

324
00:20:12,320 --> 00:20:14,000
I'm rather tired of living.

325
00:20:14,120 --> 00:20:16,800
-No, you--
-Don't! Life's precious!

326
00:20:16,880 --> 00:20:18,440
Don't do anything rash!

327
00:20:18,520 --> 00:20:20,000
This isn't settled yet!

328
00:20:20,080 --> 00:20:21,360
I can't sort this out myself,

329
00:20:21,440 --> 00:20:22,840
so I might as well jump in the river!

330
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:24,920
No, no, no! We'll help you!

331
00:20:25,120 --> 00:20:26,480
Just cover our losses!

332
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:28,160
-Words alone aren't enough
-Just cover our losses!

333
00:20:28,280 --> 00:20:29,720
to put my mind at ease.

334
00:20:29,880 --> 00:20:30,880
We'll sign an agreement!

335
00:20:30,960 --> 00:20:32,120
-Yes.
-I'll draw one up

336
00:20:32,200 --> 00:20:33,480
for you to sign and put your marks on.

337
00:20:33,560 --> 00:20:35,440
-Don't, all of you!
-Come on, come on

338
00:20:35,520 --> 00:20:37,200
-Brother! You… this…
-I'll sign it!

339
00:20:40,160 --> 00:20:41,920
My lord, shall we…

340
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:43,000
Go, go, go!

341
00:20:46,480 --> 00:20:48,320
-Come on, sign it!
-I'll do it!

342
00:20:48,400 --> 00:20:49,520
Quick! Quick!

343
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:53,640
Xie Salt Shop

344
00:20:54,240 --> 00:20:55,240
Signed!

345
00:20:55,520 --> 00:20:57,440
You, go and find out the news.

346
00:20:57,760 --> 00:20:59,720
You, go and smooth things over
with the authorities.

347
00:20:59,880 --> 00:21:01,640
And you, use your own money

348
00:21:01,880 --> 00:21:03,800
to buy back the oversold permits!

349
00:21:04,280 --> 00:21:05,280
Me?

350
00:21:06,360 --> 00:21:08,640
You-- Look carefully!

351
00:21:08,720 --> 00:21:10,320
I wasn't stupid enough to sign it!

352
00:21:10,400 --> 00:21:11,960
You're not stupid?

353
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:14,000
You walked in, gave the whole game away,

354
00:21:14,080 --> 00:21:15,880
then brought them here to collect!

355
00:21:17,160 --> 00:21:19,960
Fine. If you won't help,

356
00:21:20,440 --> 00:21:21,520
forget it.

357
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:24,560
They won't be getting
their money back either.

358
00:21:25,920 --> 00:21:27,560
-We all signed! Look!
-We all signed! Look!

359
00:21:28,720 --> 00:21:30,400
-Help us!
-Help us!

360
00:21:31,920 --> 00:21:32,920
Here.

361
00:21:39,040 --> 00:21:40,040
Go, go.

362
00:21:40,440 --> 00:21:41,440
-Quick, quick! Hurry!
-Quick, quick! Hurry!

363
00:21:42,240 --> 00:21:43,240
Not you.

364
00:21:46,480 --> 00:21:47,520
Go cook me a couple of dishes.

365
00:21:49,120 --> 00:21:50,120
What?

366
00:21:56,200 --> 00:21:57,200
PAINTINGS

367
00:21:57,280 --> 00:21:58,760
I stink of cooking fumes!

368
00:21:59,240 --> 00:22:00,840
If I didn't need her,

369
00:22:01,360 --> 00:22:03,720
I'd never be her lackey!

370
00:22:05,040 --> 00:22:06,040
My lord,

371
00:22:06,880 --> 00:22:07,880
what's so funny?

372
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:11,800
I… I'm laughing at her arrogance,

373
00:22:12,160 --> 00:22:13,640
when she may have bitten off
more than she can chew.

374
00:22:15,120 --> 00:22:16,320
Strange.

375
00:22:16,960 --> 00:22:20,000
Has her poking set my heart racing?

376
00:22:22,600 --> 00:22:23,600
Here. Take this.

377
00:22:24,560 --> 00:22:26,800
Come on.
Prod me right here.

378
00:22:27,120 --> 00:22:29,080
I… prod you?

379
00:22:29,640 --> 00:22:30,640
I wouldn't dare!

380
00:22:30,880 --> 00:22:32,760
It's all right. Go ahead--

381
00:22:32,840 --> 00:22:34,880
CALLIGRAPHY AND PAINTINGS

382
00:22:34,960 --> 00:22:36,920
My lord!
Are you all right, my lord?

383
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:38,360
You told me to prod you!

384
00:22:39,080 --> 00:22:42,320
Prod me, not kill me!

385
00:22:42,680 --> 00:22:44,440
I was too stupid to understand

386
00:22:44,520 --> 00:22:45,560
what you meant.

387
00:22:46,720 --> 00:22:49,920
Think of it as a feather,

388
00:22:50,400 --> 00:22:52,880
and prod me gently,

389
00:22:53,800 --> 00:22:57,360
while looking at me like I'm trash.

390
00:22:59,560 --> 00:23:01,760
-I see?
-I understand!

391
00:23:01,920 --> 00:23:03,200
Come on, come on. Try it.

392
00:23:03,320 --> 00:23:06,560
CALLIGRAPHY AND PAINTINGS

393
00:23:19,480 --> 00:23:20,840
Disgusting! Give it back!

394
00:23:22,600 --> 00:23:24,040
My lord! My lord!

395
00:23:24,920 --> 00:23:27,200
Wasn't my touch light as a feather,
or my look scornful enough?

396
00:23:27,360 --> 00:23:28,720
Teach me, my lord!

397
00:23:29,400 --> 00:23:31,040
Wait for me, my lord!

398
00:23:31,120 --> 00:23:32,120
Eat up.

399
00:23:35,480 --> 00:23:36,480
Eat something

400
00:23:36,640 --> 00:23:38,080
before it gets cold
and upsets your stomach.

401
00:23:39,280 --> 00:23:40,320
I don't want to eat.

402
00:23:40,400 --> 00:23:41,480
I've got no appetite,

403
00:23:41,880 --> 00:23:43,440
and my headache's getting worse.

404
00:23:44,840 --> 00:23:46,640
If only Xie Yan were here.

405
00:23:50,040 --> 00:23:51,240
Let me massage your head.

406
00:23:52,440 --> 00:23:54,400
No need. Yingtao can do it.

407
00:23:55,200 --> 00:23:56,400
Yingtao's eating,

408
00:23:56,480 --> 00:23:58,520
but I've already grabbed a few bites,
so let me do it.

409
00:24:03,080 --> 00:24:05,040
-I can eat later, my lady.
-No need.

410
00:24:05,120 --> 00:24:07,240
Go and eat so you don't go hungry.

411
00:24:07,320 --> 00:24:08,320
You eat yours.

412
00:24:16,360 --> 00:24:18,080
It's all right. I'm a doctor,

413
00:24:20,800 --> 00:24:21,800
and your friend.

414
00:24:25,680 --> 00:24:27,520
How is it? Any better?

415
00:24:27,840 --> 00:24:28,840
Thank you.

416
00:24:31,520 --> 00:24:32,640
If you're in trouble,

417
00:24:33,240 --> 00:24:34,680
I can help you think of something.

418
00:24:36,080 --> 00:24:37,680
I'm much better.

419
00:24:38,320 --> 00:24:39,360
I've been wondering

420
00:24:40,040 --> 00:24:41,200
why, when I've only just

421
00:24:41,280 --> 00:24:42,920
taken over this shop and sold

422
00:24:43,000 --> 00:24:44,720
200 or 300 permits at most,

423
00:24:45,040 --> 00:24:46,320
there are so many others out there.

424
00:24:46,560 --> 00:24:48,240
They must have been oversold

425
00:24:48,360 --> 00:24:49,680
before you took over.

426
00:24:50,600 --> 00:24:54,000
I imagine the rumors of rising prices
started then, too.

427
00:24:54,440 --> 00:24:56,120
No wonder business was so good!

428
00:24:56,560 --> 00:24:58,080
Then, as soon as the price fell,

429
00:24:58,160 --> 00:25:00,080
they came knocking with their permits.

430
00:25:01,720 --> 00:25:02,800
Such a coincidence?

431
00:25:04,880 --> 00:25:05,880
Such a coincidence?

432
00:25:06,240 --> 00:25:07,760
THE XIE ESTATE

433
00:25:07,960 --> 00:25:09,800
37, 38, 39...

434
00:25:09,880 --> 00:25:11,400
40, 41...

435
00:25:11,480 --> 00:25:12,920
You did it so quickly?

436
00:25:13,600 --> 00:25:14,760
Setting this up

437
00:25:15,120 --> 00:25:17,320
took nearly half a month,

438
00:25:17,400 --> 00:25:19,280
and plenty of silver,

439
00:25:19,480 --> 00:25:20,960
what with planting rumors

440
00:25:21,040 --> 00:25:22,520
and calling in favors.

441
00:25:22,600 --> 00:25:23,600
But at least

442
00:25:24,040 --> 00:25:25,800
I managed to drive up the price of salt,

443
00:25:25,880 --> 00:25:27,360
make a handsome profit,

444
00:25:27,440 --> 00:25:28,680
then get out.

445
00:25:29,240 --> 00:25:30,880
We took all the rewards,

446
00:25:31,640 --> 00:25:33,400
and left her to pay the price.

447
00:25:33,480 --> 00:25:36,120
You drove up the price, too?

448
00:25:38,040 --> 00:25:39,600
The salt shop's a big piece of the pie,

449
00:25:39,680 --> 00:25:41,040
but whether you can swallow it

450
00:25:41,400 --> 00:25:43,480
depends on your ability.

451
00:25:44,240 --> 00:25:46,280
She's lucky it didn't choke her!

452
00:25:46,600 --> 00:25:48,400
Once this blows up,

453
00:25:48,480 --> 00:25:50,880
that Jin woman won't handle it.

454
00:25:51,360 --> 00:25:53,080
She'll have to give it back!

455
00:25:54,520 --> 00:25:55,560
But,

456
00:25:56,320 --> 00:25:57,920
if it gets out of hand,

457
00:25:58,160 --> 00:25:59,920
and we get the shop back,

458
00:26:00,080 --> 00:26:02,400
won't we be left with the mess?

459
00:26:02,480 --> 00:26:03,880
We'll deal with it then,

460
00:26:04,400 --> 00:26:06,120
since I've got plenty of connections.

461
00:26:06,360 --> 00:26:08,640
What connections?
Why haven't I heard of them?

462
00:26:09,120 --> 00:26:11,880
You don't need to know about that.

463
00:26:12,680 --> 00:26:14,000
That Bai fellow

464
00:26:14,080 --> 00:26:16,000
was fooled into working for them, too.

465
00:26:16,800 --> 00:26:18,720
What if it leads back to you?

466
00:26:19,600 --> 00:26:20,600
So what?

467
00:26:21,200 --> 00:26:23,000
Let them investigate!

468
00:26:27,600 --> 00:26:28,880
Huaizhou docks

469
00:26:28,960 --> 00:26:30,360
Come on! Quick! Keep moving!

470
00:26:30,640 --> 00:26:31,960
Tie those mooring ropes!

471
00:26:32,360 --> 00:26:34,200
-Tight!
-All right.

472
00:26:36,560 --> 00:26:38,600
-Watch your feet!
-All right.

473
00:26:38,800 --> 00:26:40,680
-Tie that one again.
-All right.

474
00:26:43,800 --> 00:26:46,600
-My lord, all the grain...
-Come on.

475
00:26:46,800 --> 00:26:47,920
has been delivered and handed over.

476
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:49,320
As you ordered,

477
00:26:49,400 --> 00:26:52,160
we're collecting
small shipments bound for Yangzhou.

478
00:26:52,240 --> 00:26:53,760
But there aren't many,

479
00:26:53,840 --> 00:26:55,360
so the ships still aren't full.

480
00:26:55,880 --> 00:26:57,800
If you don't want to return empty,

481
00:26:58,000 --> 00:26:59,760
we'll need to wait a few days.

482
00:27:01,440 --> 00:27:03,520
-My lord, if we hurry back,
-Come on.

483
00:27:03,600 --> 00:27:05,840
and make more trips,
wouldn't we earn more

484
00:27:05,920 --> 00:27:07,080
than from these scraps?

485
00:27:08,280 --> 00:27:09,480
I know Uncle Rongchang

486
00:27:09,800 --> 00:27:11,080
always favors a quick return.

487
00:27:11,160 --> 00:27:12,200
It's a safe way to make progress,

488
00:27:12,880 --> 00:27:14,320
but if we never try anything new,

489
00:27:14,800 --> 00:27:16,200
how will we know if it's better?

490
00:27:16,720 --> 00:27:17,720
My lord,

491
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:20,280
grain deliveries have deadlines

492
00:27:20,360 --> 00:27:22,240
we simply can't miss!

493
00:27:22,360 --> 00:27:24,680
What if this extra profit

494
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:27,040
could buy another grain ship?

495
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:29,000
Then,

496
00:27:29,160 --> 00:27:31,720
you wouldn't just captain this one ship.

497
00:27:32,040 --> 00:27:33,040
Be careful!

498
00:27:37,120 --> 00:27:38,240
If he won't sail back empty,

499
00:27:38,320 --> 00:27:39,600
how long must we wait?

500
00:27:39,800 --> 00:27:41,640
If he's late, all he gets is a scolding,

501
00:27:41,720 --> 00:27:43,680
while we lose our jobs!

502
00:27:43,840 --> 00:27:45,200
-Yes!
-Yes!

503
00:27:45,280 --> 00:27:47,720
Staying away from home costs money, too!

504
00:27:48,120 --> 00:27:50,480
Who works and ends up out of pocket?

505
00:27:50,560 --> 00:27:52,560
-Exactly!
-Let's go home early!

506
00:27:52,720 --> 00:27:53,720
-Yes!
-Let's go home!

507
00:27:55,640 --> 00:27:57,160
If they pay for everything themselves,

508
00:27:57,800 --> 00:27:59,960
will they really
do their best to find shipments?

509
00:28:00,240 --> 00:28:01,680
What would you do?

510
00:28:02,320 --> 00:28:03,320
My lord,

511
00:28:04,760 --> 00:28:06,920
cover their expenses for now

512
00:28:07,000 --> 00:28:08,360
and earn their gratitude,

513
00:28:08,600 --> 00:28:11,160
so perhaps they'll do their best to help.

514
00:28:12,400 --> 00:28:13,400
With so many of us,

515
00:28:13,640 --> 00:28:15,320
managing everyone's expenses is a bother,

516
00:28:16,000 --> 00:28:17,400
and if we let them claim what they like,

517
00:28:17,480 --> 00:28:18,560
they'll overspend.

518
00:28:19,160 --> 00:28:21,400
It's better to let them pay their own way,

519
00:28:22,160 --> 00:28:23,160
since worrying about their own money

520
00:28:23,560 --> 00:28:25,480
will send them out looking for shipments.

521
00:28:26,560 --> 00:28:31,120
My lord, isn't that a little harsh?

522
00:28:32,280 --> 00:28:35,600
That's why we can't just make demands.

523
00:28:36,160 --> 00:28:37,560
Young Master Xie also says,

524
00:28:37,680 --> 00:28:38,880
whoever you are,

525
00:28:39,040 --> 00:28:41,240
if you bring in a shipment,
once the net profit's settled,

526
00:28:41,320 --> 00:28:42,440
however big or small,

527
00:28:42,560 --> 00:28:44,720
you get 20%.

528
00:28:44,960 --> 00:28:46,360
-20%!
-20%!

529
00:28:47,760 --> 00:28:48,760
-That's good!
-That's good!

530
00:28:50,320 --> 00:28:51,920
Give them something to gain, too.

531
00:28:53,240 --> 00:28:54,520
In that case,

532
00:28:54,680 --> 00:28:57,960
could I also…?
Where are you going, my lord?

533
00:28:58,040 --> 00:28:59,040
To talk business.

534
00:28:59,760 --> 00:29:02,000
SPICES FROM NORTH AND SOUTH

535
00:29:02,080 --> 00:29:04,280
I'm counting on you to ship my spices.

536
00:29:04,520 --> 00:29:05,520
Certainly.

537
00:29:05,960 --> 00:29:06,960
Don't worry.

538
00:29:16,480 --> 00:29:18,440
I wonder what Baozhu's doing now.

539
00:29:21,800 --> 00:29:23,400
Good eye, my lord!

540
00:29:29,560 --> 00:29:31,520
-Well?
-It suits Lady Jin.

541
00:29:31,600 --> 00:29:32,600
Shopkeeper,

542
00:29:32,840 --> 00:29:34,280
why are you selling this satin out here?

543
00:29:34,360 --> 00:29:35,680
Such bright reds and purples!

544
00:29:35,760 --> 00:29:36,800
I couldn't manage it all,

545
00:29:36,880 --> 00:29:38,280
so I had to clear some out and sell it.

546
00:29:38,360 --> 00:29:39,360
Want some?

547
00:29:39,600 --> 00:29:40,760
No, no, no.

548
00:29:44,320 --> 00:29:45,320
Shopkeeper,

549
00:29:45,840 --> 00:29:46,840
I'll take all of this.

550
00:29:46,920 --> 00:29:50,240
FENGRUN GRAIN SHOP

551
00:29:57,000 --> 00:29:58,640
Mr. Bai sent word

552
00:29:58,840 --> 00:30:00,000
that there are far too many salt permits

553
00:30:00,080 --> 00:30:01,840
out there, and his own savings

554
00:30:01,920 --> 00:30:02,920
won't cover them.

555
00:30:03,200 --> 00:30:04,680
He's still 200 or 300 taels short.

556
00:30:11,120 --> 00:30:13,000
I bought this with my private allowance,

557
00:30:13,080 --> 00:30:14,280
but take it to the pawnshop anyway.

558
00:30:22,560 --> 00:30:23,560
Don't worry.

559
00:30:23,640 --> 00:30:24,960
He needs you to cover his debts,

560
00:30:25,040 --> 00:30:26,600
so he won't run off with the money.

561
00:30:26,680 --> 00:30:28,120
I know,

562
00:30:28,200 --> 00:30:30,520
but I can't let go of it!

563
00:30:31,640 --> 00:30:33,720
My lady, how about wearing

564
00:30:34,080 --> 00:30:35,640
this in your hair tomorrow?

565
00:30:36,160 --> 00:30:37,480
This is for the day after tomorrow.

566
00:30:37,560 --> 00:30:39,040
I'll keep it safe tonight,

567
00:30:39,120 --> 00:30:40,320
then pawn it tomorrow morning,

568
00:30:40,400 --> 00:30:42,560
and send someone
to take the money to Mr. Bai.

569
00:30:56,880 --> 00:30:58,680
What are you doing?

570
00:31:37,920 --> 00:31:38,920
Get to work.
